 "raw_text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\n\nR30BI\n\nR30BI\n\nR30BI\n\nR30BI\n\nR3IN\n\nR3IN\n\nR3IN\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPR\n\nVEND\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nAny\n\nAny\n\nAny\n\nAny\n\nAny\n\nAny\n\nAny\n\nCOM_BUPA_MAIN_BP_INBOUND\n\nPI_BP_PROXY_BAPI_CUSTOMER\n\nPI _BP_PROXY_BAPI_ CUSTOMER\n\nPI _BP_PROXY_BAPI VENDOR\n\nCOM BUPA MWX MAP MAIN CENTRAL\n\nFSL_BUPA INBOUND FILTER IDENT\n\nFSL_ BUPA INBOUND MWX ADD ROLES\n\n8. In the S/4HANA system, activate the following function modules in the view V_BUT_CALL_FU by setting the Call indicator\nfor them. In the menu, choose |*System % Services \u00bb Table Maintenance \u00a7 Extended Table Maintenance %. The position\n\nnumbers specify the sequence in which the function modules are executed within a group with the same event and object.\nOnly the sequence of the numbers is important. That means that the absolute values of the items can be different.\n\nEvent\n\nCRMIN\n\nCRMIN\n\nCRMIN\n\nCRMOU\n\nCRMOU\n\nBPOUT\n\nObject\n\nBUPA\nBUPA\nBUPR\nBUPA\n\nBUPR\n\nBUPX\n\nItem\n\n1000000\n\n2000000\n\n1000000\n\n1000000\n\n1000000\n\n10000000\n\nFunction Module                                    Calling the\nArchiving Function\n\nBUPA_INBOUND_MAIN_CENTRAL         X\nABA_FSBP_INBOUND MAIN             X\nBUPA_INBOUND_REL_CENTRAL                 X\n\nBUPA OUTBOUND BPS FILL CENTRAL X\nBUPA OUTBOUND _BPR_FILL_CENTRAL  X\n\nMDS BUPA _OUTBOUND                           X\n\nThe events CRMOU and BPOUT are relevant for internal synchronization using CVI. In some cases, you might need additional\n\nfunction modules, such as for the event MERGE.\n\nMaking Settings for Customer/Vendor Integration\n\nContext\n\nTo synchronize customer and vendor master data with the CRM system, you use customer/vendor integration (CVI).\n\nCustomer/vendor integration synchronizes the related synchronization objects in the S/4AHANA system:\n\ne SAP business partner (BP)\n\ne Customer master record\n\ne Vendor master record\n\nYou make settings for customer/vendor integration only in the S/4HANA system.\n",
 "cleaned_text": "R30BI\n\nR30BI\n\nR30BI\n\nR30BI\n\nR3IN\n\nR3IN\n\nR3IN\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPR\n\nVEND\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nAny\n\nCOM_BUPA_MAIN_BP_INBOUND\n\nPI_BP_PROXY_BAPI_CUSTOMER\n\nPI _BP_PROXY_BAPI_ CUSTOMER PI _BP_PROXY_BAPI VENDOR COM BUPA MWX MAP MAIN CENTRAL FSL_BUPA INBOUND FILTER IDENT FSL_ BUPA INBOUND MWX ADD ROLES\n\n8 In the S/4HANA system, activate the following function modules in the view V_BUT_CALL_FU by setting the Call indicator for them. In the menu, choose |*System % Services \u00bb Table Maintenance \u00a7 Extended Table Maintenance %. The position numbers specify the sequence in which the function modules are executed within a group with the same event and object.\n\nOnly the sequence of the numbers is important. That means that the absolute values of the items can be different.\n\nEvent\n\nCRMIN\n\nCRMIN\n\nCRMIN\n\nCRMOU\n\nCRMOU\n\nBPOUT\n\nObject\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPR\n\nBUPA\n\nBUPR\n\nBUPX\n\nItem\n\n1000000\n\n2000000\n\n1000000\n\n1000000\n\n1000000\n\n10000000\n\nFunction Module | Calling the\n\nArchiving Function\n\nBUPA_INBOUND_MAIN_CENTRAL | X\n\nABA_FSBP_INBOUND MAIN | X\n\nBUPA_INBOUND_REL_CENTRAL | X\n\nBUPA OUTBOUND BPS FILL CENTRAL X BUPA OUTBOUND _BPR_FILL_CENTRAL X\n\nMDS BUPA _OUTBOUND | X\n\nThe events CRMOU and BPOUT are relevant for internal synchronization using CVI. In some cases, you might need additional function modules, such as for the event MERGE.\n\nMaking Settings for Customer/Vendor Integration\n\nContext\n\nTo synchronize customer and vendor master data with the CRM system, you use customer/vendor integration (CVI). Customer/vendor integration synchronizes the related synchronization objects in the S/4AHANA system:\n\n- SAP business partner (BP)\n\n- Customer master record\n\n- Vendor master record\n\nYou make settings for customer/vendor integration only in the S/4HANA system.",
